---
import BaseLayout from '../../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Circle from '../../components/Circle.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="PUBLIC DOMAIN SHELF" description="A curated shelf of public-domain and openly licensed sources for books, images, audio, data, and official texts.">
  <p class="back"><a href="/guides/">← Guides</a></p>

  <header class="page-head">
    <h1 class="page-title"><Circle /> PUBLIC DOMAIN SHELF</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A starting shelf, not a rights clearance service. Check the rights statement on each item and
      in your own jurisdiction before reuse.
    </p>
  </header>

  <div class="prose">
    <h2>BOOKS AND TEXTS</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.gutenberg.org/">Project Gutenberg</a> — public-domain eBooks, mostly cleared for the United States.</li>
      <li><a href="https://standardebooks.org/">Standard Ebooks</a> — carefully edited public-domain literature.</li>
      <li><a href="https://archive.org/details/texts">Internet Archive — Texts</a> — scanned books and documents with item-level rights statements.</li>
      <li><a href="https://openlibrary.org/">Open Library</a> — a catalog with borrowing and public-domain downloads.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>IMAGES AND CULTURE</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/">Wikimedia Commons</a> — freely licensed media with per-file attribution.</li>
      <li><a href="https://publicdomainreview.org/">The Public Domain Review</a> — curated essays and collections.</li>
      <li><a href="https://digitalcollections.nypl.org/">NYPL Digital Collections</a> — many public-domain items; check each record.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.loc.gov/free-to-use/">Library of Congress — Free to Use</a> — sets with rights notes.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.europeana.eu/">Europeana</a> — European cultural heritage; filter by rights.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>AUDIO AND MUSIC</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://musopen.org/">Musopen</a> — public-domain and openly licensed recordings and scores.</li>
      <li><a href="https://archive.org/details/audio">Internet Archive — Audio</a> — item-level rights vary.</li>
      <li><a href="https://freemusicarchive.org/">Free Music Archive</a> — Creative Commons music; check the license on each track.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>DATA</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/">Wikidata</a> — structured knowledge under CC0.</li>
      <li><a href="https://data.gov/">data.gov</a> — US federal open data.</li>
      <li><a href="https://data.worldbank.org/">World Bank Open Data</a> — development indicators.</li>
      <li><a href="https://www.openstreetmap.org/">OpenStreetMap</a> — map data under ODbL; attribution and share-alike apply.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>OFFICIAL TEXTS</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="https://www.rfc-editor.org/">RFC Editor</a> — Internet standards.</li>
      <li><a href="https://opensource.org/osd">Open Source Initiative</a> — the Open Source Definition.</li>
      <li><a href="https://creativecommons.org/">Creative Commons</a> — licenses and legal code.</li>
      <li><a href="https://spdx.dev/">SPDX</a> — license identifiers and SBOM standards.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>BEFORE YOU REUSE</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Find the rights statement on the item page, not just the collection page.</li>
      <li>Check the law in the country where you will publish or distribute.</li>
      <li>Keep the source URL, author, license, and access date.</li>
      <li>Do not assume “free to read” means public domain.</li>
      <li>For photographs of artworks, check the photograph's rights separately.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Read <a href="/guides/public-domain/">UNDERSTAND THE PUBLIC DOMAIN</a> and
      <a href="/guides/attribute-cc/">ATTRIBUTE CREATIVE COMMONS WORKS</a> before publishing.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
